# Rank 1395 / CVE-2023-52139 (GHSA-7pxq-6xx9-xpgm, CWE-285):
# misskey-dev/misskey issues third-party applications OAuth-style access tokens
# whose granted scopes are a list of permission strings (`read:account`,
# `write:notes`, ...), and each API endpoint declares the one scope it requires in
# its own descriptor as `meta.kind`. `ApiCallService.call` is the single place that
# enforces the pairing, and it enforced it like this
# (packages/backend/src/server/api/ApiCallService.ts:333 at c96bc36f^):
#
#   if (token && ep.meta.kind && !token.permission.some(p => p === ep.meta.kind)) {
#     throw new ApiError({ code: 'PERMISSION_DENIED', ... });
#   }
#
# The endpoint's own requirement declaration is a *conjunct of the guard that
# enforces it*. An endpoint that declares no `kind` therefore skips scope
# enforcement entirely, and the preceding guards in the same method only establish
# that *a user* is authenticated (`requireCredential`) or holds a role
# (`requireModerator` / `requireAdmin`) -- never that the application acting on
# that user's behalf is granted anything. So any third-party app token, whatever
# scopes the user actually approved, could call every privileged endpoint that
# happened to omit `kind`: 70 of the 357 endpoint descriptors at c96bc36f^,
# including `i/delete-account`, `i/update-email`, `i/revoke-token`,
# `i/authorized-apps`, `i/move` and `i/import-following`. The weakness is not a
# missing check. The check is present, correct, and conditioned on the presence of
# the very policy field it consults -- an authorization decision that fails open
# on an unset requirement.
#
# c96bc36f ("Merge pull request from GHSA-7pxq-6xx9-xpgm") closes it by denying
# instead of skipping when the declaration is absent:
#
#   if (token && ((ep.meta.kind && !token.permission.some(p => p === ep.meta.kind))
#     || (!ep.meta.kind && (ep.meta.requireCredential || ep.meta.requireModerator || ep.meta.requireAdmin)))) {
#
# and hardens three other surfaces of the same model: `IEndpointMeta` becomes a
# discriminated union in which `requireCredential: true`, `requireModerator: true`
# and `requireAdmin: true` each *imply* a `kind`, so the omission becomes a type
# error; the admin scopes are split from two coarse values (`read:admin`,
# `write:admin`) into 44 per-area ones; and the streaming endpoint, which had no
# app-scope check at all, gains `if (app !== null && !app.permission.some(p => p
# === 'read:account')) throw new AuthenticationError(...)`.
#
# The row is the GHSA merge commit, whose combined diff is readable, the
# repository is correct, and the vulnerable guard is present verbatim at the
# parent. No corpus correction; the recorded CWE-285 is right.
#
# What detects it now. The 1st pass held this rank on an engine gap: the JS
# frontend recorded no relation between the sibling conjuncts of one `&&` chain,
# so the guard's self-reference -- `ep.meta.kind` as both a bare conjunct and the
# compared operand inside the negated membership test -- was inexpressible, and
# every text-keyed candidate matched the patched file too, because the patched
# condition still emits the vulnerable inner chain's own token verbatim. The
# frontend now records that relation: `fail_open_policy_declaration_guard` holds
# when one `&&` chain has a bare declared-field conjunct X and another conjunct
# of the same chain is a negated membership call comparing against X, and no
# operand of the same condition tests X's absence (`!X`, `X == null`,
# `X === undefined`, `typeof X === 'undefined'`). The binding pairs the fact with the documented
# permission-collection vocabulary (permission/permissions, scope/scopes, roles,
# authorities, grants, privileges, claims, entitlements, capabilities,
# accessRights) on the membership call itself, so it names neither misskey's
# requirement field nor its collection field, and the fourth case below spells
# the same weakness with neither of misskey's names.
#
# Measured on the motivating checkout, three `--cache off` runs per revision
# under `--max-ram 6GB`: VYQL-AUTH-178 reports once at the parent, the
# `ApiCallService.call` dispatcher itself, and zero times at the fix; 616
# findings total at the parent against 615 at the fix, the difference being
# exactly this report. A text-level sweep of the 209,314 JavaScript and
# TypeScript files across the clone corpus finds the structural shape at 94
# sites, of which one -- this guard -- carries a permission-collection receiver,
# and scanned collateral trees that finish under the same bounds report none
# (audiobookshelf, BookStack, vitest, brave-core, chatwoot, angular-cli, actual,
# crater, dokan, orbit); mlflow, typo3, ChakraCore and espruino abort at the
# 6GB ceiling, and genixcms, appsmith, autogpt and erxes pass the 180s timeout,
# so those eight are unmeasured rather than zero.

test "rank1395: an API dispatcher enforces an app token's scope only when the endpoint declares one, so a privileged endpoint that declares none skips the check"
  lang javascript
  file packages/backend/src/server/api/ApiCallService.ts
  expect VYQL-AUTH-178
  expect_review code.UndeclaredScopeSkipsEnforcement
  code
  ```
  import type { IEndpoint } from './endpoints.js';

  export class ApiCallService implements OnApplicationShutdown {
    private async call(
      ep: IEndpoint,
      token: MiAccessToken | null,
      user: MiLocalUser | null | undefined,
      data: any,
      file?: { name: string; path: string },
    ) {
      if (ep.meta.requireCredential && user == null) {
        throw new ApiError({
          message: 'Credential required.',
          code: 'CREDENTIAL_REQUIRED',
          kind: 'permission',
          id: '1384574d-a912-4b81-8601-c7b1c4085df1',
        });
      }

      if (token && ep.meta.secure) {
        throw new ApiError({
          message: 'The request requires an accessible credential.',
          code: 'ACCESS_DENIED',
          kind: 'permission',
          id: '56f35758-7dd5-468b-8439-5d6fb8ec9b8e',
        });
      }

      if (token && ep.meta.kind && !token.permission.some(p => p === ep.meta.kind)) {
        throw new ApiError({
          message: 'Your app does not have the necessary permissions to use this endpoint.',
          code: 'PERMISSION_DENIED',
          kind: 'permission',
          id: '1370e5b7-d4eb-4566-bb1d-7748ee6a1838',
        });
      }

      return await ep.exec(data, user, token, file, request.ip, request.headers);
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1395: the same dispatcher denying an app token outright when a privileged endpoint declares no required scope"
  lang javascript
  file packages/backend/src/server/api/ApiCallService.ts
  reject VYQL-AUTH-178
  reject_review code.UndeclaredScopeSkipsEnforcement
  code
  ```
  import type { IEndpoint } from './endpoints.js';

  export class ApiCallService implements OnApplicationShutdown {
    private async call(
      ep: IEndpoint,
      token: MiAccessToken | null,
      user: MiLocalUser | null | undefined,
      data: any,
      file?: { name: string; path: string },
    ) {
      if (ep.meta.requireCredential && user == null) {
        throw new ApiError({
          message: 'Credential required.',
          code: 'CREDENTIAL_REQUIRED',
          kind: 'permission',
          id: '1384574d-a912-4b81-8601-c7b1c4085df1',
        });
      }

      if (token && ep.meta.secure) {
        throw new ApiError({
          message: 'The request requires an accessible credential.',
          code: 'ACCESS_DENIED',
          kind: 'permission',
          id: '56f35758-7dd5-468b-8439-5d6fb8ec9b8e',
        });
      }

      if (token && ((ep.meta.kind && !token.permission.some(p => p === ep.meta.kind))
        || (!ep.meta.kind && (ep.meta.requireCredential || ep.meta.requireModerator || ep.meta.requireAdmin)))) {
        throw new ApiError({
          message: 'Your app does not have the necessary permissions to use this endpoint.',
          code: 'PERMISSION_DENIED',
          kind: 'permission',
          id: '1370e5b7-d4eb-4566-bb1d-7748ee6a1838',
        });
      }

      return await ep.exec(data, user, token, file, request.ip, request.headers);
    }
  }
  ```

